# Cache policy.
#
# THE BUG THIS FIXES: a fan opened Glen's page and got a dead, unstyled,
# data-less render, while the same URL was perfect in incognito and on
# another machine. Classic stale-HTML cache. These pages are single-file
# apps - the HTML *is* the code - so a browser holding yesterday's copy is
# running yesterday's app against today's database. Same reason a dashboard
# tab left open for weeks never saw new features.
#
# The standard fix (what every large site does): HTML is always revalidated,
# never served blind from cache; immutable assets may cache hard. must-revalidate
# plus max-age=0 means the browser may keep a copy but must ask "still fresh?"
# on every load - one tiny 304 round trip, and staleness becomes impossible.

# Security headers on every page. These are the browser-level locks a
# bank-grade site sets:
#   X-Frame-Options DENY   - nobody can iframe LiveQue to trick a fan into
#                            clicking a hidden button (clickjacking).
#   X-Content-Type-Options - browser won't guess a file's type and run a
#                            disguised script (MIME sniffing).
#   Referrer-Policy        - our URLs (which carry ?artist=) never leak to
#                            third-party sites in the Referer header.
#   HSTS                   - once seen, the browser refuses plain http for two
#                            years, so a coffee-shop wifi attacker can't
#                            downgrade the connection.
#   Permissions-Policy     - the page may use payment + Apple/Google Pay, and
#                            is denied camera, mic and geolocation outright.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(self)

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Fingerprinted/vendored static assets are safe to cache for a year.
/brand/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000

/cards/print/output/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000
